d membership (D166); research groups only for ongoing matters, not for a company's own financial lines (D149/D164). Enum values come from the response schema.",
src/hivemind/prompts/role-v54.txt:21:- Open a candidate only for one of four reasons, named in opens_as. main_driver: an annual quantity that carries the company's value (the segment that carries the business, gross margin, capital spending), whether or not the company guides it, or the date by which the generation of the company's own product that carries that quantity launches or starts shipping (a carmaker's next vehicle platform; not a feature, content or software update, regional service or variant of a product already on sale); the question's ranges settle it, not a guidance figure. Not every reported or guided line. industry_aggregate: one aggregate quantity for one calendar year, such as the combined capital spending of named companies. policy_stage: a stage of a policy process, with the authority that decides it named. binding_obligation: an obligation a universe company takes on in its own name: a guarantee or credit support for another party's debt, lease or revenue, financing it extends to others, a purchase commitment or a backstop of customers' capacity or revenue, whether or not the item gives its amount; or an equity stake whose size is stated and is not yet completed. Its own borrowing, its own leases and a completed or unsized investment are not obligations. Not yet signed: a yes/no question due on a day after the item by which the signing can be checked, at most 18 months out. Already taken on, as one deal or as a programme: a financing_amount question on the amount the obligation reaches at the company's next annual filing, settled by that filing's commitments note; the announcement itself is evidence to it.
src/hivemind/prompts/role-v54.txt:37:- A research group is one ongoing matter in the world that several questions track together: a product rollout and its customer adoption, a financing or acquisition deal, a policy process, an investment or demand cycle. It usually spans companies and themes. When a candidate tracks a matter, declare the group in new_groups (local id n1, n2 …, with a name, a scope that says what is happening, and aliases: the names the matter goes by in the press, such as product, project or programme names and the parties; not company names) and cite that id in group_refs; a declared group whose names match a stored group is that group. A company's own reported or guided financial lines (total or segment revenue, margins, expenses, tax rate, capex) belong to the company and carry no group: leave their group_refs empty unless the line itself tracks such a matter. A company is not a group, and a thesis is not a group.
