tate the schema or name a list the request does not show are cut. Version 24 (2026-10-29, direct read of the v23 bench answers): entries identical to version 23; role-v24 names the item's subjects as the company, keeps another company's action only when it bears on the company's demand, supply, competition, prices or products, rejects another company's own valuation, profit or unrelated deals, a retail price or content detail, an investor's trade or the market value and unargued verdicts (standard.md section 2), tells one deal, hire or programme with its figures as one evidence item (standard section 8, judgement 11), and opens the already-taken-on obligation whether or not the item gives an amount; the duplicate links sentence is cut (the payload states it). Version 23 (2026-10-29, D237): the request is scrubbed for one company or one industry (a general hedge-fund brain): T1 drops 'such as data center and gaming', T2 reads 'trade restrictions and tariffs' for 'export controls and tariffs'; role-v23 restates every example across industries (none names a covered company or comes from a test article) and carries the standard's rules of D236 (main driver includes the launch or ship date of the product that carries the value; binding obligations; a product feature or performance detail without business scale is rejected unless a competitor sets it against the company's product; the conditional valuation is a named party's estimate; one_line names the measure). Entries otherwise as version 22. Version 22 (2026-10-28 night, D211): identical entries to version 21; the request shows no thesis and no research group (code, extraction.LEDGER_BLIND_FROM), so its bytes depend on the item alone: one sample per item in every run, no re-send in the parallel day; links name the answer's own candidates only; folds_into and lost_if_folded leave the schema; the placement call files statements under the open theses at the item's turn, matching folds a candidate into an open thesis (D19