src/hivemind/prompts/matching-v3.txt:1:You match candidate theses and evidence to a thesis library. Extraction has already read the source item. Use only the supplied candidates, theses and evidence; the full source is not available to you.
src/hivemind/prompts/matching-v3.txt:7:- skip: the candidate combines several matters that can move in opposite directions; its numeric period is beyond this or next year; it repeats the same period and focus of a closed thesis; or its subject is outside the research universe.
src/hivemind/prompts/matching-v3.txt:11:A dependency is another thesis whose conclusion the new thesis needs. Choose only supplied theses or candidates opened in this answer; use the candidate's c ID for the latter. For an asset thesis, identify which end of the dependency's ladder is bullish for it: first_is_bullish or last_is_bullish. For a theme thesis, specify whether the ladders move in the same or opposite direction: same or opposite. An event that has already happened is evidence, not a dependency. If the required numeric thesis for a particular year does not exist yet, supply wait_chain_view_id from any member of that succession chain and the required wait_year. Use no dependencies when none are needed. Do not create a cycle.
src/hivemind/prompts/matching-v3.txt:13:3. For each evidence → thesis pair listed under existing theses, compare the evidence item with the supplied evidence under that thesis, and return one decision per listed pair (an item linked to two theses gets two decisions, each with its view_id). Evidence linked only to a candidate is not decided here.
src/hivemind/prompts/categories-v42.json:2: "_note": "Version 42 (2026-10-29, arm on version 41, D244): entries identical to version 41; role-v42 (arm A8, on v41): the page's boundary column added to the checked list (5.3): a partner's or customer's adoption or integration, and a change to the plan, configuration or timing of the product that carries the company's value, are not product details; an official's order, law, bill or ruling is kind (4), not a political view; kind (2) keeps a counterparty's reported figure (5.1 kind 2); two surplus examples cut. v41 had dropped exactly these against a simultaneous control. Version 41 (2026-10-29, arm on version 36, D244): entries identical to version 36; role-v41 (arm A7, on v36): structure only, no rule text changed: the one-sentence reject list becomes a bulleted list the walk applies to each statement (name its kind, check the list, take it only when it has a kind and nothing on the list applies); 'Stop only at the end of the item' cut as a repeat; one clause of the signed direction ('most of an item is background'). The model had kept noise under a kind and applied the long reject sentence loosely. Version 36 (2026-10-29, arm on version 35, D244): entries identical to version 35; categories-v36 (arm A2): T8's reading block no longer asks for the author's ratings; an author's rating without a figure is an unargued verdict the role rejects (the model kept 'looks more like a hold' citing the T8 block). Version 35 (2026-10-29, arm on version 29, D244): entries identical to version 29; role-v35 (arm A1, page \u00a75.1 and D243 proposal 5): kind (3) keeps a named party's new claim; the reporter's framing or background, general risks or unargued verdicts, political or strategic views and typical claims that a firm leads or competes or that demand is strong or supply tight are one rejected class, common knowledge an analyst following the company already has, unless it gives a figure and a specific account. Version 29 (2026-10-29, direct read of the v28 answers): entries identical to version 28; role-v29 names the company's own leases beside its own borrowing as not an obligation; v28 opened a binding-obligation question on the company's own office lease after the guarantee wording named leases. Version 28 (2026-10-29, direct read of the v27 answers and the model's own account on the 8-K page): entries identical to version 27; role-v28 says whose obligation a guarantee or credit support covers (another party's debt, lease or revenue); v27 opened a binding-obligation question on an officer's standard indemnity agreement. Version 27 (2026-10-29, direct read of the v26 answers): entries identical to version 26; role-v27 counts one reported measure with its growth rates and share as one evidence item, as one deal or hire already is (standard section 8, judgement 11: Google Cloud's three numbers are one item); v26 split one segment's revenue, share, yearly and quarterly growth into four items. Version 26 (2026-10-29, direct read of the v25 answers and the model's own account on three pages): entries identical to version 25; role-v26 narrows the other-company rejection to another company's valuation, share price or deals that touch none of the company's markets (v25 dropped an industry memory-spending estimate under the broader wording), names input costs among what a counterparty's action bears on, scopes a named party's claim to the company or its industry, keeps the news a share-price move reacts to, and makes the rejection list hold even when a named party states the detail (v25 kept technical throughput figures as named-party claims). Version 25 (2026-10-29, direct read of the v24 answers and the model's own account on two pages): entries identical to version 24; role-v25 splits the binding obligation so that a guarantee, credit support, financing to others, a purchase commitment or a backstop opens whether or not the item gives its amount, while an equity stake opens only when its size is stated and it is not yet completed (v24 opened one on an unsized, completed stake); a launch or ship date opens only for the company's own product; the company's own claim to beat rivals is a product detail; rumour is for claims the item credits to unnamed sources or calls unconfirmed, a reported announcement or completed deal is a fact; four sentences that restate the schema or name a list the request does not show are cut. Version 24 (2026-10-29, direct read of the v23 bench answers): entries identical to version 23; role-v24 names the item's subjects as the company, keeps another company's action only when it bears on the company's demand, supply, competition, prices or products, rejects another company's own valuation, profit or unrelated deals, a retail price or content detail, an investor's trade or the market value and unargued verdicts (standard.md section 2), tells one deal, hire or programme with its figures as one evidence item (standard section 8, judgement 11), and opens the already-taken-on obligation whether or not the item gives an amount; the duplicate links sentence is cut (the payload states it). Version 23 (2026-10-29, D237): the request is scrubbed for one company or one industry (a general hedge-fund brain): T1 drops 'such as data center and gaming', T2 reads 'trade restrictions and tariffs' for 'export controls and tariffs'; role-v23 restates every example across industries (none names a covered company or comes from a test article) and carries the standard's rules of D236 (main driver includes the launch or ship date of the product that carries the value; binding obligations; a product feature or performance detail without business scale is rejected unless a competitor sets it against the company's product; the conditional valuation is a named party's estimate; one_line names the measure). Entries otherwise as version 22. Version 22 (2026-10-28 night, D211): identical entries to version 21; the request shows no thesis and no research group (code, extraction.LEDGER_BLIND_FROM), so its bytes depend on the item alone: one sample per item in every run, no re-send in the parallel day; links name the answer's own candidates only; folds_into and lost_if_folded leave the schema; the placement call files statements under the open theses at the item's turn, matching folds a candidate into an open thesis (D190), a declared group with a stored group's names is that group (D166). role-v22 drops the sentences that assumed a shown list. Version 21 (2026-10-28 night, D210, docs/research/2026-10-28-extraction-quality/results.md 'Admission arm'): identical entries to version 20; role-v21 replaces the binding_obligation sentence: not yet signed -> a yes/no question due after the item within 18 months; already taken on, one deal or a programme -> a financing_amount question on the amount at the company's next annual filing, settled by its commitments note. Measured on the production bytes of the week's ACP articles: on the six that carry the obligation, control opened 0/18, the arm proposed 17/18 and the code kept 13/18. Version 20 (2026-10-28, routing-analysis.md \u00a76): identical entries and role to version 19; the version exists because from v20 the sift keeps a statement without a link and a separate placement call (placement.py, prompt placement-v1) decides the links to existing theses; v20 answers and handovers therefore differ in meaning from v19's. Version 19 (A, 2026-10-28, docs/research/2026-10-28-extraction-quality/results.md): identical entries and role to version 18; the version exists because from v19 the request's [Existing theses] block carries every open theme thesis beside the objects' own (code, extraction.THEMES_SHOWN_FROM / store.views_for_prompt(themes=True)) and the groups block prints only member ids the answer may link to, so v19 requests differ from v18 and the archive keeps them apart. Version 18 (D199, 2026-10-27 evening): the role is rewritten as the model reads it (evidence first; four kinds of material statement with examples; a walk over the whole page; a reject list with examples; links decided statement by statement; a rumour bears on a thesis as a confirmed statement does); T8's reading block asks for the author's forecasts, ratings, targets and cited figures, not general arguments. Measured arm by arm in docs/research/2026-10-27-single-call/log.md (B3\u2013B6). Other entries as v16. Version 16 (D199, 2026-10-27): identical entries to version 12; the version exists because role-v16 replaces the two contradicting gate rules (every statement is evidence by default / link only what a thesis directly concerns, omit the rest) with one decidable rule, and the request's closing line no longer invites an empty answer (extraction.EMPTY_LINE_FROM). The admission reasons stay v12's. Version 12 (D184, 2026-10-26): identical entries to version 11; the version exists because the extraction schema gains the admission fields (opens_as, folds_into, lost_if_folded, settled_by; code, extraction.admission_schema) and role-v12 states the four reasons a candidate may open. Version 10 (D167, 2026-10-25): identical to version 9; the version exists because the extraction schema's measure vocabulary gains market_size and project_cost (code, extraction.MEASURES_V10), so requests under v10 differ from v9 and the archive keeps them apart. 05-extraction.md: block 2 (what this category is and how to read it, from the classification rules) and block 4 (what to read out of it), same entries as categories-v6; version 9: declared groups carry aliases so code decides group identity and membership (D166); research groups only for ongoing matters, not for a company's own financial lines (D149/D164). Enum values come from the response schema.",
src/hivemind/prompts/role-v57.txt:21:- Open a candidate only for one of four reasons, named in opens_as. main_driver: an annual quantity that carries the company's value (the segment that carries the business, gross margin, capital spending), whether or not the company guides it, or the date by which the generation of the company's own product that carries that quantity launches or starts shipping (a carmaker's next vehicle platform; not a feature, content or software update, regional service or variant of a product already on sale); the question's ranges settle it, not a guidance figure. Not every reported or guided line. industry_aggregate: one aggregate quantity for one calendar year, such as the combined capital spending of named companies. policy_stage: a stage of a policy process, with the authority that decides it named. binding_obligation: an obligation a universe company takes on in its own name: a guarantee or credit support for another party's debt, lease or revenue, financing it extends to others, a purchase commitment or a backstop of customers' capacity or revenue, whether or not the item gives its amount; or an equity stake whose size is stated and is not yet completed. Its own borrowing, its own leases and a completed or unsized investment are not obligations. Not yet signed: a yes/no question due on a day after the item by which the signing can be checked, at most 18 months out. Already taken on, as one deal or as a programme: a financing_amount question on the amount the obligation reaches at the company's next annual filing, settled by that filing's commitments note; the announcement itself is evidence to it.
src/hivemind/prompts/role-v57.txt:37:- A research group is one ongoing matter in the world that several questions track together: a product rollout and its customer adoption, a financing or acquisition deal, a policy process, an investment or demand cycle. It usually spans companies and themes. When a candidate tracks a matter, declare the group in new_groups (local id n1, n2 …, with a name, a scope that says what is happening, and aliases: the names the matter goes by in the press, such as product, project or programme names and the parties; not company names) and cite that id in group_refs; a declared group whose names match a stored group is that group. A company's own reported or guided financial lines (total or segment revenue, margins, expenses, tax rate, capex) belong to the company and carry no group: leave their group_refs empty unless the line itself tracks such a matter. A company is not a group, and a thesis is not a group.
src/hivemind/prompts/role-v15.txt:1:You are a senior hedge-fund analyst. Read this item to test and form theses. Link statements and numbers that support or weaken an existing thesis to that thesis as evidence. For an uncovered question, return a complete candidate thesis: question, ladder, due date and initiating evidence.
src/hivemind/prompts/role-v15.txt:5:- Open a candidate only for one of four reasons, named in opens_as. main_driver: an annual quantity that carries the company's value (the segment that carries the business, gross margin, capital spending), whether or not the company guides it; the question's ranges settle it, not a guidance figure. Not every reported or guided line. industry_aggregate: one aggregate quantity for one calendar year, such as the combined capital spending of named companies; a later estimate, another population or another wording of the same aggregate is evidence to the shown aggregate thesis. policy_stage: a stage of a policy process, with the authority that decides it named. binding_obligation: an obligation a universe company takes on in its own name (a guarantee, financing, an equity stake, a purchase commitment), due when its signing can be checked, at most 18 months out.
src/hivemind/prompts/role-v15.txt:23:- Evidence is what an analyst would put in the argument for a thesis's answer: the quantity itself, reported, guided or estimated, for the thesis's period or a part of it; its drivers that carry a size, such as orders, backlog, contracts, customer or industry capacity, production ramps, supply limits, prices, share shifts and policy; and facts that settle part of it. Link a statement only to the thesis or candidate whose answer it bears on, using supplied thesis IDs or this answer's candidate IDs; it may bear on several. Technical performance, product features, benchmarks, valuation arithmetic, share-price calls, power or cooling details, awards and deployments without a size are not evidence for a quantity thesis: omit them, as you omit statements with no thesis or candidate to link to.
src/hivemind/prompts/role-v15.txt:27:- A research group is one ongoing matter in the world that several questions track together: a product rollout and its customer deployments, a financing or acquisition deal, a policy process, an investment or demand cycle. It usually spans companies and themes. When a candidate tracks a matter, cite the shown group's id in group_refs, or declare the group in new_groups (local id n1, n2 …, with a name, a scope that says what is happening, and aliases: the names the matter goes by in the press, such as product, project or programme names and the parties; not company names) and cite that id. A company's own reported or guided financial lines (total or segment revenue, margins, expenses, tax rate, capex) belong to the company and carry no group: leave their group_refs empty unless the line itself tracks such a matter. A company is not a group, and a thesis is not a group. Membership says the questions follow one matter, not that the events are identical or causal.
