e version exists because from v19 the request's [Existing theses] block carries every open theme thesis beside the objects' own (code, extraction.THEMES_SHOWN_FROM / store.views_for_prompt(themes=True)) and the groups block prints only member ids the answer may link to, so v19 requests differ from v18 and the archive keeps them apart. Version 18 (D199, 2026-10-27 evening): the role is rewritten as the model reads it (evidence first; four kinds of material statement with examples; a walk over the whole page; a reject list with examples; links decided statement by statement; a rumour bears on a thesis as a confirmed statement does); T8's reading block asks for the author's forecasts, ratings, targets and cited figures, not general arguments. Measured arm by arm in docs/research/2026-10-27-single-call/log.md (B3\u2013B6). Other entries as v16. Version 16 (D199, 2026-10-27): identical entries to version 12; the version exists because role-v16 replaces the two contradicting gate rules (every statement is evidence by default / link only what a thesis directly concerns, omit the rest) with one decidable rule, and the request's closing line no longer invites an empty answer (extraction.EMPTY_LINE_FROM). The admission reasons stay v12's. Version 12 (D184, 2026-10-26): identical entries to version 11; the version exists because the extraction schema gains the admission fields (opens_as, folds_into, lost_if_folded, settled_by; code, extraction.admission_schema) and role-v12 states the four reasons a candidate may open. Version 10 (D167, 2026-10-25): identical to version 9; the version exists because the extraction schema's measure vocabulary gains market_size and project_cost (code, extraction.MEASURES_V10), so requests under v10 differ from v9 and the archive keeps them apart. 05-extraction.md: block 2 (what this category is and how to read it, from the classification rules) and block 4 (what to read out of it), same entries as categories-v6; version 9: declared groups carry 