src/hivemind/prompts/role-v31.txt:30:- A research group is one ongoing matter in the world that several questions track together: a product rollout and its customer adoption, a financing or acquisition deal, a policy process, an investment or demand cycle. It usually spans companies and themes. When a candidate tracks a matter, declare the group in new_groups (local id n1, n2 …, with a name, a scope that says what is happening, and aliases: the names the matter goes by in the press, such as product, project or programme names and the parties; not company names) and cite that id in group_refs; a declared group whose names match a stored group is that group. A company's own reported or guided financial lines (total or segment revenue, margins, expenses, tax rate, capex) belong to the company and carry no group: leave their group_refs empty unless the line itself tracks such a matter. A company is not a group, and a thesis is not a group.
src/hivemind/prompts/role-v18.txt:7:- Decide links statement by statement, never for the page as a whole. A statement bears on a thesis when its figure or fact changes what that thesis's answer will be: a customer's order of 18,000 Blackwell chips bears on the data center revenue thesis; a CPU server order bears on the stand-alone CPU revenue thesis; a renewal price for older GPUs bears on the gross margin thesis; an expert's view on political dependence bears on none. Link it to that thesis or those theses, by the supplied thesis ids or this answer's candidate ids; a customer's, supplier's or competitor's page is read for the company's demand, pricing and margin theses. A rumour or an unconfirmed report bears on a thesis exactly as a confirmed statement does: the tier records the confidence, the link records the bearing. Never link a statement to a thesis it does not bear on because no better thesis is shown: keep it with empty links.
src/hivemind/prompts/role-v18.txt:16:- Open a candidate only for one of four reasons, named in opens_as. main_driver: an annual quantity that carries the company's value (the segment that carries the business, gross margin, capital spending), whether or not the company guides it; the question's ranges settle it, not a guidance figure. Not every reported or guided line. industry_aggregate: one aggregate quantity for one calendar year, such as the combined capital spending of named companies; a later estimate, another population or another wording of the same aggregate is evidence to the shown aggregate thesis. policy_stage: a stage of a policy process, with the authority that decides it named. binding_obligation: an obligation a universe company takes on in its own name (a guarantee, financing, an equity stake, a purchase commitment), due when its signing can be checked, at most 18 months out.
src/hivemind/prompts/role-v18.txt:32:- A research group is one ongoing matter in the world that several questions track together: a product rollout and its customer deployments, a financing or acquisition deal, a policy process, an investment or demand cycle. It usually spans companies and themes. When a candidate tracks a matter, cite the shown group's id in group_refs, or declare the group in new_groups (local id n1, n2 …, with a name, a scope that says what is happening, and aliases: the names the matter goes by in the press, such as product, project or programme names and the parties; not company names) and cite that id. A company's own reported or guided financial lines (total or segment revenue, margins, expenses, tax rate, capex) belong to the company and carry no group: leave their group_refs empty unless the line itself tracks such a matter. A company is not a group, and a thesis is not a group. Membership says the questions follow one matter, not that the events are identical or causal.
